00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.320
Theory Number 1: The Fate of Henry Bowers.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.020
As a child, Henry Bowers is the most feared
bully in town, terrorizing the Losers Club

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.970
with his gang of thugs and his switchblade.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.090
His mental stability deteriorates towards
the end of the summer, when he kills his father

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.930
and goes after the Loser’s Club to try to
kill them as well.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.250
As an adult, Henry plays a significant part
in the book.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.440
He’s broken out of a mental asylum by It
to seek revenge.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.790
But in It: Chapter 1, Henry is bested by Mike,
who knocks him into the well in the basement

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.010
of 29 Neibolt, which looks to go on forever.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.780
This has led many to believe that the second
film will be taking a different approach.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.010
But before I talk about my thoughts on how
Henry might have survived, let me show you

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:52.800
