00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.670
So how did Henry Bowers survive the fall in
the wellhouse?

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.600
We’ve already seen that It has the power
to transfigure parts of the house, so I think

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:01.079
it stands to reason that it could have created
some kind of net, or something to catch Henry.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:05.080
Henry had already proven himself a worthy
servant by killing off his father at the request

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.700
of Pennywise and in a deleted scene and killing
his two friends, Victor and Belch.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.450
If we take that to be canon, then it might
not really work for either of them to be the

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:18.110
form that It uses to break Henry out of the
asylum, so maybe Henry never actually left

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.110
Derry.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.200
I think it’s kind of a creepy idea to consider
that It kept Henry down in the sewers all

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.730
those years, just waiting to unleash his minion
again 27 years later.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.940
Theory Number 2: We discover the origin of
It.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.190
In 1990, the first adaptation of It was released
in the form of a 2-part TV mini-series.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:38.890
Understandably, with the novel coming in at
over 1100 pages, some of those scenes had

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.480
to be left out, one of which was the smoke-hole
scene, where the members of the Loser’s

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.160
Club attempt to carry out an ancient Native
American ritual to help them decide what they

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.050
should do about their Pennywise problem.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:51.739
The ritual involves them starting a campfire
in their underground fort and breathing in

00:02:51.739 --> 00:02:54.370
the smoke until they have a vision telling
them what to do.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:57.410
If that sounds familiar, you may have already
read the book, or maybe you just hung out

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.320
with the wrong kids in high school, I don’t
really know.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.099
But when they carry out the ritual, everyone
jumps out for air except Richie and Mike,

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:07.210
and they see their tiny clubhouse expand,
and then the smoke clears and they find themselves

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:10.830
in the middle of the Barrens, but the landscape
is different and they are surrounded by animals

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.800
that haven’t lived in Maine for thousands
of years.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.590
Now I’m not going to spoil anything, but
they basically see the arrival of It.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.031
This scene takes place when they’re kids,
and it’s obviously not in Chapter 1, but

00:03:20.031 --> 00:03:22.810
just because we didn’t see it in the movie
doesn’t mean it didn’t happen.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:26.440
We’ve already seen in the trailer that there
will be flashbacks to when they were all children,

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.300
and the majority of the adult portion of the
novel is their forgotten childhood memories

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.440
coming back to them.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.489
So I think we could either see a smoke-hole
scene as a flashback in Chapter 2, or another

00:03:35.489 --> 00:03:36.970
scene that explains Pennywise’s origins.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:40.580
Based on the trailer, it already looks like
there’s going to be some backstory on Pennywise’s

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:45.100
human form, Bob Gray, which is the name Pennywise
uses to introduce itself to several characters

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.800
in the book such as Georgie, Eddie and Beverly.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.110
My third theory pertains to the final form
of It.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:54.130
Now obviously there’s no way I can do this
one without going into spoilers, so if you

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.840
haven’t seen the mini-series or read the
book, it’s a quick enough read isn’t it?

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.970
You can just breeze through that puppy in…
uh… an hour or two?

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.290
So when it comes to the 1990 adaptation, the
most common complaint by far is the final

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:10.629
spider form, it’s probably the least scary
part making everything feel a bit anticlimactic.

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:14.291
And it’s just following the book, but in
the book King is able to explain that it’s

00:04:14.291 --> 00:04:18.359
not really a spider, and that that’s just
the closest thing our tiny human brains can

00:04:18.359 --> 00:04:19.400
interpret It as.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.119
But the response to the mini-series spider
has led some to believe that the filmmakers

00:04:23.119 --> 00:04:26.180
behind It: Chapter 2 are going to take it
in a different direction.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:30.039
We have seen them setup a possible showdown
between It and Bill, which is known as The

00:04:30.039 --> 00:04:33.330
Ritual of Chud in the book, where Bill is
launched outside of his physical body into

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.139
this thing called The Macroverse, where he
basically has to defeat It with his mind,

00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:40.660
with the guidance of another celestial being
known as The Turtle, who is also teased at

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.199
and referenced in Chapter One.

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:51.460
“It’s a turtle!”

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:56.569
However, unlike the smoke hole scene, it's
not like that’s something that could have

00:04:56.569 --> 00:04:58.880
happened but it just wasn’t shown in the
first movie.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.309
We see the final battle and that doesn’t
happen.

00:05:01.309 --> 00:05:05.599
But what does happen is Pennywise temporarily
transforms into a half-arachnid creature while

00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:06.969
cycling among forms.

00:05:06.969 --> 00:05:10.819
I have to think this is a little tease that
the second movie will stay true to the idea

00:05:10.819 --> 00:05:13.909
of It’s final form appearing as a spider
to the Losers.

00:05:13.909 --> 00:05:17.819
However, I don’t think that necessarily
means that it’s going to be anticlimactic

00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:22.150
again, I just think they have to make a cooler
looking arachnid than the one from 1990.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:26.099
Maybe instead of a giant spider, it’s more
of a half clown, half spider alien hybrid.

00:05:26.099 --> 00:05:29.210
I always thought it was strange that we’re
haunted by a clown for the whole story, but

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.800
then at the end it’s just a spider all the
sudden, so I think incorporating the clown

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.550
into the spider form be a more fitting conclusion.

